<title>USA: Study finds U.S customers frustrated with insurers.</title>
<headline>Study finds U.S customers frustrated with insurers.</headline>
<byline>Patricia Vowinkel</byline>
<dateline>WHITE SULPHUR SPRINGS, W.V. 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>A national survey of about 2,000 corporate buyers of insurance found that they were frustrated with their insurers and unhappy with the products and services they receive.</p>
<p>The survey, conducted by the Quality Insurance Congress (QIC) over the last year, showed &quot;there is a significant gap between the system of insurance and customers' expectations,&quot; said Jay Deragon, executive director of the QIC in Nashville, Tenn.</p>
</text>
